    "usage": {
      "status": "verified",
      "verifiedAt": "2026-06-10",
      "resultPull": "sync",
      "auth": "none",
      "callShape": "DEFAULT backend (x402-gateway): POST JSON {\"text\":\"<string>\",\"model\":\"text-embedding-3-small\"}; for batch use {\"texts\":[\"a\",\"b\"],\"model\":...}. ALTERNATE backend (orthogonal, https://x402.orth.sh/openai/embeddings): OpenAI-native body {\"input\":\"<string or array>\",\"model\":\"text-embedding-3-small\"} (optional encoding_format, dimensions, user). The two gateways are NOT body-compatible — sending OpenAI {input:...} to the railway gateway returns 400 and still charges; sending {text:...} to orth.sh will fail validation (it requires input+model).",
      "inputExample": {
        "text": "hello world",
        "model": "text-embedding-3-small"
      },
      "outputShape": "DEFAULT backend (x402-gateway): NON-OpenAI flat shape — embedding (number[1536]) at top level, i.e. response.embedding[]; batch likely returns response.embeddings[][]. ALTERNATE backend (orthogonal): standard OpenAI shape — data[].embedding (number[]), model, usage.prompt_tokens, usage.total_tokens (it proxies to api.openai.com/v1/embeddings).",
      "quirks": [
        "FIELD-NAME TRAP differs per backend: x402-gateway uses 'text' (single string) or 'texts' (array) and REJECTS the OpenAI 'input' field; orthogonal uses the OpenAI 'input' field. Pick the body shape for the backend you actually call.",
        "x402-gateway: sending {input:...} returns HTTP 400 'Provide text (string) or texts (array of strings)' AND still charges you $0.001.",
        "OUTPUT shape differs per backend: x402-gateway returns {embedding:[...]} at top level (NOT OpenAI's {data:[{embedding}]}). orthogonal returns the real OpenAI envelope {data:[{embedding,index}],model,usage}.",
        "x402-gateway verified live returns a 1536-dimension float vector for text-embedding-3-small.",
        "Pricing: x402-gateway $0.001 (x402 v2), orthogonal $0.003 (x402 v1). Default to the cheaper railway gateway unless you need the OpenAI-native envelope/'input' field.",
        "x402-gateway accepts USDC on Base (eip155:8453), USDm (eip155:4326), and Solana USDC. orthogonal accepts USDC on Base only (x402 v1).",
        "Pass 'dimensions' to reduce vector size (text-embedding-3 only); supported on the orthogonal/OpenAI body, default model text-embedding-3-small."
      ],
      "needs": [],
      "needsApproval": false,
      "guide": "Generate text embedding vectors with OpenAI text-embedding-3-small (1536 dims) for semantic search, clustering, classification and RAG. Same model offered via two x402 gateways; pick the body/output shape that matches the chosen backend. DEFAULT backend (x402-gateway): POST JSON {\"text\":\"<string>\",\"model\":\"text-embedding-3-small\"}; for batch use {\"texts\":[\"a\",\"b\"],\"model\":...}. ALTERNATE backend (orthogonal, https://x402.orth.sh/openai/embeddings): OpenAI-native body {\"input\":\"<string or array>\",\"model\":\"text-embedding-3-small\"} (optional encoding_format, dimensions, user). The two gateways are NOT body-compatible — sending OpenAI {input:...} to the railway gateway returns 400 and still charges; sending {text:...} to orth.sh will fail validation (it requires input+model). Output: DEFAULT backend (x402-gateway): NON-OpenAI flat shape — embedding (number[1536]) at top level, i.e. response.embedding[]; batch likely returns response.embeddings[][]. ALTERNATE backend (orthogonal): standard OpenAI shape — data[].embedding (number[]), model, usage.prompt_tokens, usage.total_tokens (it proxies to api.openai.com/v1/embeddings).",
